# ==============================================================
# OCEAN PUZZLE - INSTRUCTIONS: ROOM 4 (The Ancient Instrument)
# ==============================================================
# Script type : interact
# Bind to     : [FILL IN: x y z of the clickable head block]
# Map/area    : [FILL IN: map name / room]
# Import      : /s i i <paste URL>, then click the head block
#
# What it does:
#   The Oracle explains the final instrument puzzle.
#   Can be replayed once every 45 seconds per player.
#
# Requires: puzzle1 namespace (see Submit script header)
# Related scripts: Instructions Rooms 1-2 and 3 (share the same cooldown)
# ==============================================================
@using puzzle1
@define Long now = system::currentTimeMillis()

@if oracle_ready_at > now
    @define Long seconds = (oracle_ready_at - now + 999L) / 1000L
    @player &cOracle: You must wait {{seconds}} seconds to hear the instructions again.
    @return
@fi

@var oracle_ready_at = now + 45000L

@player &3Oracle: &bTen signs return to you, each bearing a voice heard in a chamber before.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bSet each note to the voice its sign first revealed.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bYet pitch alone will not shape the song. Each sign carries a hidden worth.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bLet that worth guide their procession: the lightest claim speaks first, the heaviest last.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bCarry the song you uncover to the waiting instrument in this chamber.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bTune its ten voices, then sound the melody swiftly, before the moment slips beneath the tide.
@delay 3s
@player &3Oracle: &bRemember what you heard. Remember what each sign is worth. The sea remembers both.
